1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,290
Stare for 20 seconds and your hand wriggles?

2
00:00:04,340 --> 00:00:06,060
Stare at the dot in the middle
of the spiral for 20 seconds

3
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:07,430
Then look at the hand picture → your real hand

4
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:10,000
Stop right away if you feel dizzy

5
00:00:10,050 --> 00:00:18,770
Don't take your eyes off the center dot

6
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:25,770
Just a little longer!

7
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:30,770
Keep looking at the center when it ends

8
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:33,940
Is the hand swelling and wriggling?

9
00:00:33,990 --> 00:00:37,910
Now look at your real hand!

10
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,880
Motion-sensing cells are two teams
playing tug of war

11
00:00:39,930 --> 00:00:41,650
When they pull equally,
still things look still

12
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:43,917
Watch inward motion for 20 seconds
and the "inward" team gets tired

13
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:48,217
So when you look at something still,
the "outward" team wins — it seems to swell!

14
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:50,187
Stare at a waterfall, then look at a rock…

15
00:00:50,237 --> 00:00:53,987
The rock seems to move up —
that is the waterfall illusion!

16
00:00:54,037 --> 00:00:56,037
It goes back to normal in a moment

17
00:00:56,087 --> 00:00:59,237
NEXT: A black-and-white picture in color?
